>>Turn 127690 - YAAP.

> What were you doing all that time?

Very carefully exploring every inch of Gehennon.

I don't know what these people who talked about Nethack being "too
generous" are thinking.  There were still a number of items on my
personal shopping list that I still hadn't found when I first went into
Gehennon:

1) Gauntlets of power.
2) Magicbane (wishes for it failed, which might mean it was somewhere
in the dungeon).
3) Scroll of gold detection -- at least one.
4) more magic markers. (My armor class when I entered Gehennon was in
the -20s, and I wanted it to be substantially better).
5) Magic harp (carries several taming charges and can be re-charged
with scroll of charging. A marvelous tool on Astral, as if a monster
summoning happens you simply play it once or twice and you've got a
pack of bodyguards).
6) Tengu for inherent teleport control.
7) Ring of conflict.
8) Ring of free action.
9) scroll of taming (at least one).
10) more scrolls of genocide.  (I later wished and wrote for some, but
only because I
hadn't found what I needed.)
11) More gold (I figured I might anger my deity, and in that case would
need to buy protection back again. It's happened before).
12) And of course, spares of everything irreplaceable.

Patient and careful exploration of Gehennom over a period of 4
real-time nights
gained me items 3,4,7, 8, one of 10, and 11.  This rounded out my
ascension kit which had previously been considerably lacking. To be
honest, I don't know how to do a speed ascension, as I simply never
have all the tools I need.


